# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Copy to .env.local for local dev. For the Vercel deploy, set these in the
#  Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) instead.
#  All NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are baked into the client bundle at build time and
#  are PUBLIC — never put a secret in one. See DEPLOYMENT.md.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Base URL of the real Kobo backend API. Unset (or empty) => the app runs
# entirely against the mock data/API layer in lib/kobo/*.
#   Local dev:  NEXT_PUBLIC_KOBO_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
#   Vercel:     NEXT_PUBLIC_KOBO_API_URL=https://api.kobopayments.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KOBO_API_URL=

# MoonPay publishable key (pk_test_… / pk_live_…). Used by the browser to ask
# MoonPay which IP it observes (/v4/ip_address) before Add Funds, so the backend
# can IP-lock the widget URL only when its own view agrees. Must match the
# backend's MOONPAY_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. It's a publishable key — already public in
# every widget URL — safe in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MOONPAY_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...

# Crossmint client-side key (ck_staging_…), for the "Card / Apple Pay" Add
# Funds option (CrossmintEmbeddedCheckout — see
# components/kobo/onramp/crossmint-checkout-modal.tsx). Console pre-req: this
# key's allowed origins must include every real front-end origin
# (https://kobopayments.com + this host's local dev origin) — see the KOBO —
# CROSSMINT FRONTEND INTEGRATION report's Step 5 founder console pre-reqs.
# A client-side key is designed to be exposed in browser code — safe in a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ var, unlike the backend's server-side CROSSMINT_API_KEY.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CROSSMINT_CLIENT_KEY=ck_staging_...

# Real `users.id` (uuid) and wallet_address of the app's default/pre-selected
# recipient ("Adaeze Okonkwo" — name/subtitle stay hardcoded display fixtures,
# only the id/wallet are real), created via POST /users with role: "recipient".
# Required in real mode. Same value locally and on Vercel.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KOBO_DEFAULT_RECIPIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KOBO_DEFAULT_RECIPIENT_WALLET=

# ⚠️ LOCAL-ONLY, NEVER on Vercel. Skips the login/PIN flow with a seeded user
# and a visible "dev bypass" banner (companion to backend DEV_SKIP_AUTH). Must
# be left UNSET in the Vercel project or the deployed app ships with auth
# bypassed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SKIP_AUTH=true
